            "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"staged-query/v0.6\",\"decision\":\"request_query\",\"query_attempt\":{\"question\":\"What does DefaultApplicationFactory do from line 130 onward: how do getHealthUrl, getManagementBaseUrl, getEndpointsWebPath, and getManagementBaseUrl's port/context-path helpers compose the management and health URLs, and where does PathMappedEndpoints (or webEndpoint base path) enter the computation?\",\"scenario_id\":\"cloudfoundry_application_uri_base_url\",\"tool\":\"inspect_source\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"operation\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"source_id\\\":\\\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":130,\\\"end_line\\\":185}\"},\"previous_receipt_assessment\":{\"impact\":\"supports\",\"rationale\":\"The search returned real body lines for the only remaining unknown area: DefaultApplicationFactory line 147 declares getHealthUrl(), and lines 148-149 show it first returns instance.getHealthUrl() when that is non-null. Since the test's InstanceProperties sets only a name and never a health URL, the asserted 'http://application/Uppercase/actuator/health' must be composed further below, which locates the exact region still needed and confirms the fallback path is the one exercised.\",\"evidence\":[{\"source_id\":\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\",\"start_line\":147,\"end_line\":149}]},\"impact\":\"The pending read targets the precise region (lines 130-185) where getHealthUrl, getManagementBaseUrl and the endpoints-web-path helper are defined, which determines the PathMappedEndpoints interactions the hidden stub must satisfy for the asserted management and health URLs.\",\"stop_explanation\":null,\"question_updates\":[{\"question_id\":\"q1\",\"question\":null,\"goal_indexes\":null,\"impact\":null,\"rationale\":\"Still open: getHealthUrl's fallback and getEndpointsWebPath have not been read yet, and those bodies decide what the hidden PathMappedEndpoints stub must return. The search now pinpoints getHealthUrl at line 147, so a bounded read of 130-185 is expected to close this.\",\"evidence\":[{\"source_id\":\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\",\"start_line\":147,\"end_line\":149},{\"source_id\":\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\",\"start_line\":118,\"end_line\":130}],\"state\":\"open\",\"acquisition\":\"available\",\"attempted_sequences\":[1,2,3,4,5,6]}],\"candidate_updates\":[{\"scenario_id\":\"cloudfoundry_application_uri_base_url\",\"description\":\"CloudFoundryApplicationFactory scenario: inject a PathMappedEndpoints stub and default Instance/Server/Management/WebEndpoint properties plus a metadata contributor and empty CloudFoundryApplicationProperties; then set a single URI 'application/Uppercase' and call createApplication, expecting management URL 'http://application/Uppercase/actuator', health URL 'http://application/Uppercase/actuator/health', service URL 'http://application/Uppercase/', name 'test' and metadata 'contributor'='test'. Production behavior already observed: getServiceBaseUrl is overridden to prepend 'http://' to the first configured URI; getServiceUrl appends '/' via UriComponentsBuilder; getManagementUrl appends '/' plus getEndpointsWebPath to getManagementBaseUrl; and getHealthUrl returns instance.getHealthUrl() only when set, so the asserted health URL comes from the fallback composition. Because InstanceProperties carries no service/management/health URLs in the test, the base URLs must resolve through server/management properties and the health path must come from the endpoints web path supplied by the PathMappedEndpoints stub.\",\"evidence\":[{\"source_id\":\"mut\",\"start_line\":42,\"end_line\":50},{\"source_id\":\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\",\"start_line\":70,\"end_line\":81},{\"source_id\":\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\",\"start_line\":97,\"end_line\":125},{\"source_id\":\"repository:f1cbe4e7534b595de231fa4a\",\"start_line\":147,\"end_line\":149},{\"source_id\":\"test\",\"start_line\":45,\"end_line\":57}]}]}"
